# E-1102: We say that $A\subseteq \mathbb{N}$ has property $P$ if, for all $n\geq 1$, there are only finitely many $a\in A$ such that $n+a$ is squarefree. We say that $A$ has property $Q$ if there are infinitely many $n$ such that $n+a$ is squarefree for all $a<n$. How fast must sequences $A=\{a_1<a_2<\cdots\}$ with properties $P$ or $Q$ increase?
